    "readme": "# Calendar event index evidence\n\n[Contract](../../../../docs/specs/calendar-event-index-info.md) \u00b7 [Generated records](../../../calendar/demo-event-indices.json) \u00b7 [Handoff](../../../../docs/wiki/investigations/integrated-source-and-factory-proof-2026-10-09.md)\n\n- RED `a4159ce53`: independent proof records 0 PASS / 9 FAIL, exit101. First configured lookup reaches public getter/arity but fails DTO type; validation test accepts missing required input. Later snapshot/security assertions were unreached. No compile/setup failure.\n- Producer `fa66dd878`: owned position map, normal default seeding, location filters, fresh DTOs and documented secret-input authentication. GREEN receipts report 11 PASS / 0 FAIL, including update/removal and cleanup restoration. Independent GREEN verification PASS; [report](green/green-independent-report.md).\n- Normal loaded simulator: real `rawget` publication/demo assertions followed by Lua-error collection, exit0/`[]`. No third-party addons or SavedVariables; not full Calendar UI acceptance.\n- Final default `cargo check` and `cargo fmt --check`: exit0; source scope recorded. Manual changed-Rust readability found no violations. Six inherited manifest deprecation warnings remain; not suppressed.\n- Current gap change `296b9ac77` removes only event-index publication row after normal loaded publication assertion. Initial integration-target selector executed zero tests, not proof; retained under `publication-zero-selection/`. Correct owning `prefork_full_ui` target reports one exact publication case PASS, classifying 145 identities (89 OK / 56 known gaps); Calendar raw/lookup publication is OK. Independent publication/retention verification pending. Frozen historical87OK/58gaps is unchanged.\n\n`retention-manifest.json` lists 48 nonbinary copies/172,495bytes. No executable, library, vendor tree, cache payload or native Calendar capture retained. Reuse independent RED authentication; do not infer native ID representation, catalog/lifecycle behavior or whole-handoff completion. Frozen broad suite3FAIL remains separate.\n"
